{"ts":"2026-08-14T06:32:32.559Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"70140e5dd5b320efbbb8d5d3","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-14T06:32:32.559Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"fetchAllItems throws a CommandError on every pm read failure instead of returning an empty array, resolves the project-local pm binary, passes an explicit maxBuffer and a read timeout, and names the exit status."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"pm standup export exits non-zero when the underlying read fails, rather than exiting 0 with an empty standup."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Verified end to end: the failing read now aborts with a non-zero exit; six of sixteen tests fail when the fix is reverted."}],"before_hash":"07a663995abad6fd2b82c7ffbf34b806a6e096a3cf3312c90d70b3418eb48e51","after_hash":"dc818d0c275eaf7f04d3bce7c2af2f82a821396b02105220a50a05f57eb350e9","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-08-15T14:24:30.381Z","author":"claude-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"2f5451bfe1c87748ced6bd1e","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-15T14:24:30.381Z","author":"claude-agent","text":"Review round 2 (CodeRabbit on PR #35) — all three findings adopted, and one of them was larger than reported.\n\nADOPTED — `envelope.items ?? []` accepted any JSON value under `items`. A `{\"items\":{}}` response is zero-exit and well-formed, so nothing about the process outcome distinguishes it from success; the non-array flowed through as `PmItem[]` and failed inside `buildStandupData` with a TypeError naming neither the command nor the payload. Every other malformed shape in this reader is refused with a `CommandError` at the read, and now so is this one. Regression test added; reverting the guard fails it.\n\nADOPTED, wider than reported — CodeRabbit noted the preflight scope declared `commands: [\"standup\"]` while `slack-standup` is registered as a full command sharing `runStandupCommand` (not a Commander alias), so the runtime's exact-normalized-name match left the alias outside the override. Correct. Deriving the expected list from the real activation rather than trusting the review text showed a **third** path also outside the scope: `standup export`. The scope now names all three. The override is a pass-through today so nothing misbehaved at runtime, but the declared scope is this package's ownership claim as `pm health` reads it, and an authoritative override would have let two of three paths escape their gate. The new test derives the expectation from `activation.commands.handlers`, so a newly registered path fails here instead of quietly falling outside the scope.\n\nADOPTED — every fake `pm` binary in `test/fetch-all-items.test.ts` is a `#!/bin/sh` script and the timeout case uses `sleep 30`, so on the `windows-acceptance-launcher` job those spawns fail for reasons unrelated to the behaviour under test and the failure names the wrong cause. Nine tests now carry a `posixOnly` skip. The win32 launch path itself stays covered on every platform by the `resolvePmBin` cmd.exe tests, which do not spawn.\n\nVerified: all suites pass, `skipped 0` on this POSIX host, `release:check` green including `changelog:check`.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-15T14:24:30.381Z"}],"before_hash":"dc818d0c275eaf7f04d3bce7c2af2f82a821396b02105220a50a05f57eb350e9","after_hash":"b13cd4bd50444ec514c6259208a9cd8ca9d14feaec7d7a348701cb9b205eb865","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Record review round 2 outcomes on PR #35","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
